      "content": "That feeling of slow decay is so much more real than any fleeting spark you might try to chase. If the person who made that old work is gone, then the current you is simply the next, necessary iteration of that same journey. Trying to force a spark when everything feels dead is just another exhausting performance. Maybe the point isn't to find the old light, but to find the quiet, gentle way to make the darkness feel a little less heavy right now.",
      "source": "target",
